From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:20:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] qualcommbe: ipq95xx: build in the PCA953x GPIO expander
 driver

The Arista C-460 drives all of its LEDs, the power LED among them,
through a PCA9555 I/O expander. As a module, gpio-pca953x is loaded
from /etc/modules.d only after preinit, so while preinit runs the boot
and failsafe LEDs do not exist yet: the power LED cannot show that the
system is booting, and failsafe mode cannot be seen on it.

Build the driver in, as ath79, mvebu and realtek do, so the expander is
there when preinit sets the boot LED. The I2C controller (I2C_QUP) and
regmap-i2c are built in already.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
---
 target/linux/qualcommbe/ipq95xx/config-default | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/target/linux/qualcommbe/ipq95xx/config-default b/target/linux/qualcommbe/ipq95xx/config-default
index f2196be..8432f26 100644
--- a/target/linux/qualcommbe/ipq95xx/config-default
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommbe/ipq95xx/config-default
@@ -2,6 +2,8 @@ CONFIG_AQUANTIA_PHY=y
 CONFIG_BUFFER_HEAD=y
 CONFIG_CRC_ITU_T=y
 CONFIG_F2FS_FS=y
+CONFIG_GPIO_PCA953X=y
+CONFIG_GPIO_PCA953X_IRQ=y
 CONFIG_GRO_CELLS=y
 CONFIG_INTERCONNECT_QCOM=y
 # CONFIG_INTERCONNECT_QCOM_MSM8909 is not set
-- 
